    <name>
      <text>Evaluating an Integral by the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to evaluate</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int _{@lower_limit@}^{@upper_limit@}{@quest_expr@}\,dt\)</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Recall: \( \displaystyle \int x^n dx=\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+c\)</p>
<p></p>
<p>Using this rule we'll have:</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle 
\int _{@lower_limit@}^{@upper_limit@}{@quest_expr@}&=\left [ {@soln1@} \right ]_{@lower_limit@}^{@upper_limit@}\\
                                                                                &= {@ta1@}\\
\end{align}
\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
